Changes: bring resident Aff2 rejection down into the baseline layer; restore MSM8916's physical-primary-zero policy in preboot while retaining MSM8939 dense primary lookup; add tests that cover all listed primaries and missing CPUs. Document unresolved IOMMU ordering concern rather than blindly hoist TLBI.

Source review: pinned pem120/linux45add32603ee4aa28979ad6ec70c10b14af4ac29 drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c assigns domain pointers before loop (239-240), restores secure config and disables old context within loop (252-271), enables SCTLR.M (295-307), then the checked-in patch invalidates/syncs before publishing pgtbl_ops. A pre-loop helper call has valid pointers/ASIDs, but precedes secure restore/context disable; an active old context could refill stale translations after that early invalidation. Current enable-to-invalidate window is a source-confirmed risk, not a captured device DMA event. No safe zero-window sequence is established here; no IOMMU code changed.
https://github.com/pem120/linux/blob/45add32603ee4aa28979ad6ec70c10b14af4ac29/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c#L239-L320
MSM8916's existing0006 patch uses the same post-program position. Existing A5 evidence supports keeping invalidation, not a guarantee against transient active DMA.

CodeRabbit pb_setup finding is false: actual insertion is smp_spin_table_cpu_prepare, not cpu_init. setup_arch invokes smp_init_cpus; later kernel_init_freeable invokes smp_prepare_cpus. Exact pinned source: arch/arm64/kernel/smp.c490-503,740-821; arch/arm64/kernel/setup.c357-359; init/main.c1006-1011,1646-1660.

